\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O love, who formedst me to wear
\par The image of Thy Godhead here;
\par Who soughtest me with tender care
\par Through all my wanderings wild and drear:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O Love, I give myself to Thee,
\par Thine ever, only Thine to be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O Love, of wisdom is truth and light,
\par The Word and Spirit, life and power,
\par Whose heart was bared to them that smite,
\par To shield us in our trial hour:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O Love, I give myself to Thee,
\par Thine ever, only Thine to be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Love, who thus hast bound me fast,
\par Beneath that gentle yoke of Thine;
\par Love, who hast conquered me at last,
\par And rapt away this heart of mine:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O Love, I give myself to Thee,
\par Thine ever, only Thine to be.
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par \'b6 Verse 4
\par \ulnone\b0 4. O Love, who once shalt bid me rise
\par From out this dying life of ours;
\par O Love, who once above yon skies
\par Shalt set me in the fadeless bowers:
\par 
\par \ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O Love, I give myself to Thee,
\par Thine ever, only Thine to be.
\par \cf1\ul\b\f1 
\par \f2 
\par }

